WEBVTT

00:00.610 --> 00:03.180
Solve for a and
check your solution.

00:03.180 --> 00:06.054
And we have a plus
5 is equal to 54.

00:06.054 --> 00:07.470
Now, all this is
saying is that we

00:07.470 --> 00:10.310
have some numbers,
some variable a.

00:10.310 --> 00:13.484
And if I add 5 to
it, I will get 54.

00:13.484 --> 00:15.400
And you might be able
to do this in your head.

00:15.400 --> 00:17.820
But we're going to do it a
little bit more systematically.

00:17.820 --> 00:19.570
Because that'll be
helpful for you when we

00:19.570 --> 00:21.070
do more complicated problems.

00:21.070 --> 00:23.361
So in general, whenever you
have an equation like this,

00:23.361 --> 00:24.930
we want to have the variable.

00:24.930 --> 00:29.670
We want this a all by itself
on one side of the equation.

00:29.670 --> 00:31.360
We want to isolate it.

00:31.360 --> 00:32.819
It's already on
the left-hand side,

00:32.819 --> 00:34.360
so let's try to get
rid of everything

00:34.360 --> 00:35.490
else on the left-hand side.

00:35.490 --> 00:37.490
Well, the only other thing
on the left-hand side

00:37.490 --> 00:38.580
is this positive 5.

00:38.580 --> 00:42.440
Well, the best way to get rid
of a plus 5, or a positive 5,

00:42.440 --> 00:44.910
is to subtract 5.

00:44.910 --> 00:46.300
So let's subtract 5.

00:46.300 --> 00:50.110
But remember, this says
a plus 5 is equal to 54.

00:50.110 --> 00:52.180
If we want the
equality to still hold,

00:52.180 --> 00:54.430
anything we do to the left-hand
side of this equation,

00:54.430 --> 00:57.550
we have to do to the right
side of the equation.

00:57.550 --> 01:00.660
So we also have to
subtract 54 from the right.

01:00.660 --> 01:03.090
So we have a plus 5 minus 5.

01:03.090 --> 01:05.030
Well, that's just
going to be a plus 0.

01:05.030 --> 01:08.080
Because if you add 5 and you
subtract 5, they cancel out.

01:08.080 --> 01:10.400
So a plus 0 is just a.

01:10.400 --> 01:14.520
And then 54 minus 5, that is 49.

01:14.520 --> 01:15.220
And we're done.

01:15.220 --> 01:16.975
We have solved for a.

01:16.975 --> 01:19.460
A is equal to 49.

01:19.460 --> 01:20.810
And now we can check it.

01:20.810 --> 01:24.270
And we can check it by
just substituting 49 back

01:24.270 --> 01:27.100
for a in our original equation.

01:27.100 --> 01:29.600
So instead of writing a
plus 5 is equal to 54,

01:29.600 --> 01:32.040
let's see if 49 plus
5 is equal to 54.

01:32.040 --> 01:34.010
So we're just
substituting it back in.

01:34.010 --> 01:39.920
49, 49 plus-- let me do that
in that same shade of green.

01:39.920 --> 01:43.730
49 plus 5 is equal to 54.

01:43.730 --> 01:45.270
We're trying to check this.

01:45.270 --> 01:48.210
49 plus 5 is 54.

01:48.210 --> 01:51.140
And that, indeed,
is equal to 54.

01:51.140 --> 01:54.080
So it all checks out.
